HRX Product Requirements Document (PRD)
Version 1.0 | Status: Draft, ready for build | Product: HRX, an AI-assisted employee management and HR platform
1. Overview
HRX is a role-based web application that centralizes employee records, attendance, leave, payroll records, documents, performance reviews, notifications, analytics, reports and bounded AI assistance for small and medium organizations. It is built as a deployable, portfolio-grade system: realistic enterprise behavior, understandable architecture, one developer.
Stack decisions (fixed): React + TypeScript + Vite (web), Node.js + Express 5 + Mongoose (API), MongoDB Atlas, Cloudinary (files), Google Gemini (AI, behind a provider abstraction), Socket.IO (real-time), deployed to Vercel (web) and Render (API).
2. Problem statement
Small and medium organizations manage employee data, attendance, leave, documents, payroll records and performance information across disconnected spreadsheets, shared folders, email and manual approvals. This causes duplicated data, slow approvals, weak access control, no audit trail, and no consolidated view for decision-making.
HRX replaces this with one system that has role-based access, an audit trail, real-time notifications, role-specific dashboards, and AI help that is explicitly advisory.
3. Goals and non-goals
Goals
1. Give each role a single place to do its HR work with the minimum number of clicks.
2. Enforce data access on the server so employees can only see their own sensitive data and managers only their direct reports.
3. Make approvals (leave) and reviews (performance) visible in real time to the people affected.
4. Provide trustworthy reporting and analytics scoped by role.
5. Provide AI assistance that is useful, grounded in company policy, and cannot bypass permissions.
6. Ship a deployable, tested, documented system.
Non-goals
• Statutory payroll, tax, PF/ESI or other compliance calculation. Payroll is a management/demo module.
• Recruitment, applicant tracking, onboarding workflows, expense claims, shift scheduling.
• Biometric, QR or GPS attendance (future extension only).
• Mobile native apps (the web app is responsive).
• Multi-tenant SaaS billing. HRX serves one organization per deployment.
• Automated employment decisions of any kind.
