12. Risks and mitigations
Risk
Mitigation
Scope too large for one build
Priority tiers and phased delivery with a verification gate after each phase
Refresh cookie blocked across Vercel and Render domains
Proxy /api through Vercel rewrites so the cookie is first-party; document fallbacks
Authorization gaps (IDOR)
Central permission map and scoping helpers; negative tests for every resource
AI hallucinates policy
Answer only from stored policies; refuse when unsupported; show references
Prompt injection or data leakage via AI
Authorization decided in code; minimal data sent to the model; injection tests
Malicious file upload
Allowlist, magic-byte check, size limits, private storage, signed URLs
Render free-tier cold starts affect Socket.IO and first requests
Document the limitation; reconnect handling; optional paid tier
Third-party service limits (Gemini, Cloudinary, Atlas free tiers)
Configurable model and limits; graceful errors; document quotas
Payroll mistaken for compliant payroll
Clear non-statutory labelling in UI and docs
13. Assumptions and dependencies
• One organization per deployment; a single organization timezone.
• A Monday to Friday work week is the default and is configurable.
• Accounts needed for deployment: MongoDB Atlas, Cloudinary, Google AI (Gemini), Render, Vercel, GitHub.
• Policy content for the assistant is seeded sample data and is replaced by the organization's real policies.
• Demo credentials exist for development only; the seed script refuses to run in production.
